-**ORCA decision.** We chose to indicate 150 shares at the $28 upper bound. Under the scenario’s stated lognormal valuation model, the expected valuation premium is approximately 14.6%, with approximately a 25% probability of finishing below the offer. We limited the indication to our intended position rather than inflating the bid to offset pro-rata allocation. The October 24 live log shows 111 ORCA shares at a $28 average entry.
+**ORCA decision.** We chose to indicate 150 shares at the $28 upper bound. The model is defined in `engine/exchange/ipo.py`: `POP_MU=0.12`, `POP_SIGMA=0.18`. It gives `exp(0.12 + 0.18²/2) - 1 = 14.59%` expected valuation premium and `Φ(-0.12/0.18) = 25.25%` probability of value below the offer. We limited the indication to our intended position rather than inflating the bid to offset pro-rata allocation. The October 24 live log shows 111 ORCA shares at a $28 average entry.
 
